|Activity|Verdict|Strive for|How not to act|
|---|---|---|---|
|Marriage|Practice|Faithfulness, partnership, and care; the Stoic Musonius Rufus called marriage a full sharing of life|Treating your spouse as furniture; flirting elsewhere; keeping score|
|Parenting|Practice|Teach by example, as Socrates made his companions better by being good himself (Memorabilia I.2.3); correct your children when they value money over virtue (Apology 41e)|Parenting by screen; anger as discipline; wanting children to look successful more than to be good|
|Parents and family|Practice|Gratitude to your parents despite their faults, as Socrates taught Lamprocles; make the first move with estranged siblings|Holding grudges; listing their failures while forgetting what they gave you|
|Friendship|Practice|Few, good friends; ask what you're worth to them (Memorabilia II.5); help in practical ways|Friendships for use or status; disappearing when a friend is in trouble|
|Gossip|Avoid|Speak of people as if they were present; Epictetus advised above all not to talk about other people, praising, blaming, or comparing (Handbook 33)|Talking behind backs; sharing others' failures for entertainment|
|Anger|Avoid|No anger at all: the one who wrongs you errs unwillingly, so there is nothing to be angry at; ask, as Socrates asked the man beating his servant, which of you deserves correction|Venting on those beneath you: employees, waiters, children, anyone who can't answer back|
|Honesty|Practice|Say what's true, plainly, even when it costs you, as Socrates did with Critias and the jury|White lies for convenience; flattery; staying silent to avoid trouble|
|Conflict|Practice fairly|Question rather than attack; seek the truth together|Winning at the cost of truth; humiliating the other person|
|Forgiveness|Practice|Let go of resentment, as Socrates did with his judges|Nursing grudges; revenge, which Socrates rejected even for wrongs done to you|$q$, 266, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$interpretive$q$]::text[], true),
