|Activity|Verdict|Strive for|How not to act|
|---|---|---|---|
|Citizenship|Practice|Do your civic duties faithfully, as Socrates did as a soldier and as a presiding officer; obey the law, and refuse orders that are clearly unjust|Ignoring your community; or treating politics as a team sport where your side can do no wrong|
|Politics and public opinion|In moderation|Form views carefully, know the facts, as Socrates asked of Glaucon, and hold them with humility|Tribal anger; certainty without knowledge; letting opinions of the crowd decide yours, which Cleanthes told Stoics to ignore|
|Reputation|Not up to you|Be good and let reputation follow or not|Managing your image; doing good for credit; fearing what others think more than doing right|
|Status and ambition|In moderation|Seek responsibility when you can do it well, as Socrates urged Charmides|Chasing titles, followers, or prestige; ambition beyond your competence, as Glaucon's was|$q$, 135, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$interpretive$q$]::text[], true),
